<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pentri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pentri were the largest and most powerful of the four Samnite peoples of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, living in the mountains of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molise">Molise</a> around their chief town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bovianum">Bovianum</a>. The great sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietrabbondante">Pietrabbondante</a> lay in their territory. They led Samnite resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the Samnite Wars and again in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a> of 91–88 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pentri.jpg" alt="Pentri" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TCI Cartographic Office · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Archeological_sites_I_1992_-_Siti_archeologici_del_Sannio_e_del_Molise_-_Touring_Club_Italiano_CART-TEM-092_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
